{number: 134}
{title: Lord, I’m Coming Home}
{key: C}

{start_of_verse: 1}
[C] I've wandered far a-[F] way from [C] God,
Now I'm coming [G7] home;
The [C] paths of sin too [F] long I've [C] trod,
[G7] Lord, I'm coming [C] home.
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_chorus}
[C] Coming home, [F] coming [C] home,
Nevermore to [G7] roam;
[C] Open wide Thine [F] arms of [C] love,
[G7] Lord, I'm coming [C] home.
{end_of_chorus}

{start_of_verse: 2}
[C] I've wasted many [F] precious [C] years,
Now I'm coming [G7] home;
I [C] now repent with [F] bitter [C] tears,
[G7] Lord, I'm coming [C] home.
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_verse: 3}
[C] I'm tired of sin and [F] straying, [C] Lord,
Now I'm coming [G7] home;
I'll [C] trust Thy love, be-[F] lieve Thy [C] Word,
[G7] Lord, I'm coming [C] home.
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_verse: 4}
My [C] only hope, my [F] only [C] plea,
Now I'm coming [G7] home;
That [C] Jesus died, and [F] died for [C] me,
[G7] Lord, I'm coming [C] home.
{end_of_verse}
